The Inquisition is a convox of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]]. It builds cases against perversions against the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] or the Church, and then acts on them. It is a convox in name, but its work keeps it outside the Church's normal chain of command: in theory it reports to the Pontifex, and in practice it runs itself. The Church's own people avoid it unless they have good reason to deal with it.

Its office in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] carries a ten-foot metal sign out front: the Host's three-wave emblem, wrapped in chains. Inside it runs more like an office and waiting room than a precinct, and the night desk is manned by an Inquisitor rather than a receptionist. Below the lobby are questioning rooms with plain stone walls.

Inquisitors are remade by training and rituals the Church does not perform on just anyone. Each comes out strange in their own way.
